  System.Runtime.Unicode.adam - The Unicode facts print's text specs read
  (M3.8f4): libc++'s extended grapheme cluster break property and indic
  conjunct break property tables (the cluster rules, System.Runtime's
  DoCluster*), its estimated width table (a cluster's columns) and its
  escaped output table (the debug form `?`), each with its lookup as libc++
  writes it (an upper bound search over packed ranges).

  GENERATED by scripts\adam\gen_fmt_tables.py from libc++'s __format headers
  (extended_grapheme_cluster_table.h, indic_conjunct_break_table.h,
  width_estimation_table.h, escaped_output_table.h); never hand-edited: a
  newer libc++ is a rerun of the script.
  The same on every target; imports nothing. System.Runtime imports it.
*******************************************************************************/

